        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: влюблённый",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "влюблённый (vlyublyónnyy) — \"in love; a lover\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Влюблённые гуляли по парку до утра. Vlyublyónnyye gulyáli po párku do utrá. The lovers walked in the park until morning."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "From влюбиться — to fall in love. Влюблён в кого — in love with someone."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "влюблённый (vlyublyónnyy) is the past participle of влюбиться 'to fall in love', built on в 'into' and любить 'to love'; EtymDB lists the participle without a source."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
