              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "поцелуй (potselúy) — \"a kiss\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Она на всю жизнь запомнила первый поцелуй. Oná na vsyu zhizn zapómnila pérvyy potselúy. She remembered her first kiss for the rest of her life."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine; genitive поцелуя. The verb is целовать — to kiss."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "поцелуй (potselúy) is built on целовать 'to kiss', which EtymDB traces to Proto-Slavic cělovati 'to greet; to kiss', derived from cělъ 'whole', as if a kiss once wished someone good health; EtymDB has no entry for поцелуй (potselúy)."
            }
          ]
        },
